     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Deploying mfa:admin alone blocks exfiltration. Each exfiltration path needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup. Each of those needs a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three require stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those in turn need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which can only come from auth_dc or auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa_admin deployed, the chain breaks and exfiltrated can never become true. Zero controls is not enough. With no defences, the attacker can phish_workstation, pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and then exfiltrate_db. So the minimum is 1.\"}"
    }
